@page "/"
@using Portfolio.Client.Components

<PageTitle>Oliwer Karlsson — Software Developer</PageTitle>

<section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Software Developer</p>
        <h1>Oliwer Karlsson</h1>
        <p class="lead">
            Fullstack developer in Gothenburg. I work across the stack in C#, JavaScript
            and Java — building things, breaking them, and working out why. This site is
            one of them: Blazor WebAssembly on the front, Azure Functions behind it,
            running serverless at no cost.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#projects">See projects</a>
            <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#contact">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="about" class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <h2><span class="section-marker accent-red"></span>About</h2>

        <p class="section-body">
            I'm a fullstack developer from Gothenburg, and I got here by being curious
            about how things work and stubborn about finding out.
        </p>

        <p class="section-body">
            I graduated from Teknikhögskolan in 2026 with top grades in every course, and
            have worked on an education platform building features across the frontend and
            backend, where I also served as Scrum Master. I'm currently driving freight
            trains while I move into development full time.
        </p>

        <p class="section-body">
            Most of what I know I learned by building something that didn't exist yet.
            Right now that's WhereIsFood, a live map of Gothenburg's food trucks. Before
            that it was a real-time quiz app, mostly to find out how WebSockets behave when
            a room full of people are answering at once.
        </p>

        <p class="section-body">
            Outside work I train Muay Thai, poke at cybersecurity on TryHackMe, and I've
            been learning game development in Unity — no finished game yet, just working
            out how a different kind of engine thinks. The security side isn't what I'm
            looking to do professionally, but it changes how you build: you start assuming
            someone will send you something you didn't expect.
        </p>

        <p class="section-body">
            I'm looking for a developer role where I'll be pushed to learn things I don't
            know yet.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="projects" class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <h2><span class="section-marker accent-green"></span>Projects</h2>
        <p class="section-body">
            Things I've built, and the reasoning behind them.
        </p>

        <div class="project-grid">
            <ProjectCard Title="WhereIsFood"
                         Kicker="In progress · 2026"
                         AccentClass="accent-red"
                         Href="/projects/whereisfood"
                         Summary="A live map of Gothenburg's food trucks, weighing how much to trust each location update and saying so in plain language."
                         Tech="@(new[] { "TypeScript", "Next.js", "Postgres", "MapLibre" })" />

            <ProjectCard Title="Database seeding system"
                         Kicker="Professional work · 2025–26"
                         AccentClass="accent-green"
                         Href="/projects/seeding"
                         Summary="Reproducible test data for a live education platform, built at Klarr and the subject of my thesis."
                         Tech="@(new[] { "JavaScript", "Express", "MongoDB", "AJV" })" />

            <ProjectCard Title="This portfolio site"
                         Kicker="Live · 2026"
                         AccentClass="accent-blue"
                         Href="/projects/portfolio"
                         Summary="Serverless portfolio on the Microsoft stack, built to run at zero cost and treat its own public API as hostile input."
                         Tech="@(new[] { "C#", ".NET 8", "Blazor", "Azure" })" />

            <ProjectCard Title="Real-time quiz app"
                         Kicker="Learning project · 2025"
                         AccentClass="accent-yellow"
                         Href="/projects/quiz"
                         Summary="Kahoot-style multiplayer quiz with room-based WebSocket sync, deployed and run on EC2."
                         Tech="@(new[] { "JavaScript", "Socket.IO", "Next.js", "AWS" })" />
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="certificates" class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <h2><span class="section-marker accent-yellow"></span>Certificates</h2>
        <p class="section-body">
            Verified through Credly — click any badge to check it.
        </p>
        <Certificates />
    </div>
</section>

<section id="contact" class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <h2><span class="section-marker accent-blue"></span>Contact</h2>
        <p class="section-body">
            Got a question or an opportunity? Send me a message below, or email me directly at
            <a href="mailto:oliwer.carlsson.jobb@gmail.com">oliwer.carlsson.jobb@gmail.com</a>
            if you'd rather keep a copy of what you sent.
        </p>
        <ContactForm />
    </div>
</section>
